        <footnote id="F1">On October 23, 2026, upon effectiveness of the Issuer's resale registration statement on Form S-3, all 65,001 shares of Series A Convertible Preferred Stock held directly by Univest Securities LLC, together with accrued and unpaid dividends through October 15, 2026, automatically converted into 1,422,472 shares of the Issuer's common stock at a conversion price of $0.9129 per share. Univest Group, Inc. is the parent holding company of Univest Securities LLC and owns all of its outstanding equity interests. Yi (Edric) Guo is the Chief Executive Officer of Univest Securities LLC and owns approximately 49.7% of the outstanding Class A Common Stock of Univest Group, Inc. As a result of these relationships, Mr. Guo may be deemed to beneficially own the securities held directly by Univest Securities LLC. Mr. Guo disclaims beneficial ownership of such securities except to the extent of his pecuniary interest therein, if any.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">Each share of Series A Preferred Stock had a liquidation value of $18.2580 and was convertible based on a conversion price of $0.9129 per share of Common Stock. The 1,422,472 shares of Common Stock issued upon conversion represented the 1,300,020 shares of Common Stock initially underlying the 65,001 shares of Series A Preferred Stock, plus additional shares attributable to accrued and unpaid dividends through October 15, 2026.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">The Series A Preferred Stock was convertible at the holder's election at any time on or after its date of issuance and had no stated expiration date.</footnote>
